thinking
**Analyzing pattern config and label selection compatibility**

I’m checking how the new pattern config structure handles cases where users override to include only a subset of patterns. I notice that the current label resolution demands patterns for all taxonomy labels, which causes errors if some are missing. To fix that, I plan to make the resolver skip missing base configs when possible but still error if label selection references unavailable labels. This should allow valid subsets without breaking defaults.
